    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0536" n="462" xml:id="pg462"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Williams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-10-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 13, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 11th of July last, No.
                    4, transmitting a copy of the correspondence which passed between yourself and
                    Prince Kung upon the subject of the assassination of the late President Lincoln,
                    has been received. The sentiments expressed by his excellency regarding the
                    melancholy occurrence referred to are highly appreciated.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wells Williams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
